	(text "EoS TM4C123 Board, rev A, BoosterPack-compatible (40-pin). Designed by Kartikeydheer Srivastava.\nCopyright (c) 2026 Kartikeydheer Srivastava. All rights reserved; see LICENSE.txt.\nValues from TI SPMS376E (TM4C123GH6PM) and SPMA059; Silicon Labs CP2102N Rev. 1.5; Diodes DS37274; Littelfuse SP05xxBA;\nNDK NX3225GA; Abracon ABS07; Nexperia BAT54J; onsemi MMBT3904; Wurth 150141M173100; Kingbright.\nFirmware: set OSCDRV (C14/C15 20 pF); USB as a forced device, VBUS on PB3;\nunlock PF0 and PD7 (GPIOLOCK 0x4C4F434B, GPIOCR) before using them.\nJP1 (one shunt): 1-2 device port powers the board, 2-3 debug port; do not feed J3.21 with JP1 fitted,\nnor J1.1 ever (3.3 V output). 3.3 V budget 300 mA in all, about 225 mA of it for BoosterPacks.\nCP2102N on 3.3 V; R31 bleeds VDBG so its VBUS pin reads low with no debug host. J3.29/J3.30, PB2 open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
